# UX workflow: guarded Project source deletion with named impact.
# Purpose: proves that an early release is an exact Cancel and a completed hold
# deletes one source plus exactly its two assignments as one Undoable action.
# Expect: capture_changed:modulators_registry=delete_impact_armed, capture_changed:delete_impact_armed=delete_cancelled, capture_changed:delete_cancelled=delete_impact_committing, capture_changed:delete_impact_committing=source_deleted
# Expect: semantic:delete_cancelled:effect=delete_modulator, semantic:delete_cancelled:outcome=cancelled
# Expect: semantic:source_deleted:effect=delete_modulator, semantic:source_deleted:outcome=applied, semantic:source_deleted:operation_generation=1

0 scenario project-modulators
100 button LEFT_CENTER down
700 encoder NAV 1
780 encoder NAV 2
860 encoder NAV 3
940 encoder NAV 4
1020 encoder NAV 5
1100 button LEFT_CENTER up
1320 capture screen modulators_registry

# First hold: the impact names Slow Tide and its two destinations; release
# before completion must keep the graph intact and state that it was cancelled.
1440 button BOTTOM_LEFT down
1740 capture screen delete_impact_armed
2040 button BOTTOM_LEFT up
2260 capture screen delete_cancelled

# Second hold crosses the guard fully, then release commits the scoped delta.
2440 button BOTTOM_LEFT down
2780 capture screen delete_impact_committing
3700 tick
3780 button BOTTOM_LEFT up
4020 capture screen source_deleted
